    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2NHHvYc3HmHawMRAQ8ZBRyF)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Independent of other open PRs; touches only `sp-litnotes-meta.el`, its doc and its tests.\n- If merged after a PR that edits the same module (e.g. further `sp-litnotes-meta` changes), expect a conflict in `sp-litnotes-meta.org` / `.el`; resolve by keeping both.\n\n## What and why\n\nSia asked that `sp-litnotes-meta-fill` (single and `-fill-all-convert` batch) never deletes fields, only adds or modifies.\n\n- Audited every path in `sp-litnotes-meta.el` that removes, empties or rewrites meta (fill, `--set`, `--put`, the unquote step, the type tag, the key sort, the bib-parent/pub-title lints, the `(none)` choice from #473).\n- Found and fixed:\n  - **Real loss:** with `sp-litnotes-meta-update-changed` (default t) a `pub-author`/`pub-editor` with more names than BibTeX (a co-author added by hand) was replaced by the BibTeX list, dropping the extra name. `--differs-p` now says \"no difference\" when the note has more names.\n  - `--put` with nil/empty replaced a value by nothing. `--set` and `--put` now ignore blank values; only `sp-litnotes-meta--allow-clear`, bound by the *remove* choice of `sp-litnotes-meta-parent-lint-convert` (a per-note choice with backup), empties a line.\n  - `--set` added a new line right after the last item's first line, splitting a continuation line from its item; it now goes after the continuation lines.\n- Checked, no change needed: empty and `(none)` answers (`bib-project`, `relevance-factor`, `read-priority`, `read-status`) give nil and leave the note alone; the key sort and the type tag only move or extend; `--tidy-new-note` (drops `#+print_bibliography`) runs only for newly created notes, not in a fill.\n- **Safeguard:** before saving, `sp-litnotes-meta-fill` compares the note with its text from before (`sp-litnotes-meta--lost`). A fewer lines of a key, a value now empty, a non-blank line gone, or a filetag gone refuses the write, restores the buffer and signals `sp-litnotes-meta-lost-data`. In the batch that is one failed note in the results; the rest are still filled.\n- The existing dry run (`sp-litnotes-meta-fill-all-dryrun`) already writes nothing; I did not add another one.\n- Doc: bullets under \"Design choices\" in `docs/tangles/academic/sp-litnotes-meta.org`.\n- No CHANGELOG edit (nightly tidy).\n\n## How I checked\n\n- Emacs 29.3 in batch: `sp-litnotes-meta-test.el`, 78 tests pass (69 before, 9 new). The tangle check (`tools/check-tangle.sh`) is green.\n- New tests: batch convert on a note with unknown keys, a repeated key, a multi-value `pub-author` with a continuation line, an empty value, a `(none)` value and extra tags: all remain, the differing title/year are modified, the backup equals the original; `(none)`/empty answers add nothing; blank values are ignored; new lines go after continuation lines; a deliberately buggy step that deletes a line or a filetag is refused with the note and buffer restored (file and visited buffer), and in the batch it is listed as a failure while the other note is filled.\n\n## Not tested\n\n- Not run on the real vault, real citar-vulpea or real Vulpea (all stubbed).\n- A person line with more names than BibTeX is now kept even when you wanted BibTeX to win; use the note itself to fix it.\n- Batch dry run does not preview a refusal (it only happens at write time).\n\n## Manual testing checklist\n\n- [ ] Copy a few real litnotes (one with extra keys, one with two authors and a hand-written co-author) to a scratch folder or commit them first.\n- [ ] `M-x sp-litnotes-meta-fill-all-dryrun`: the list looks as before; a note with an extra co-author no longer lists \"update pub-author\".\n- [ ] `M-x sp-litnotes-meta-fill-all-convert`, answer `(none)` or empty to all questions: `git diff` on the notes shows only additions and corrected title/year/pages.\n- [ ] Diff the backup folder `litnote-meta-backups/<time>/` against the notes: no line missing except those intentionally modified.\n- [ ] A note with a multi-line `pub-author` item and a missing `pub-year`: the new line goes after the continuation line.\n- [ ] `M-x sp-litnotes-meta-parent-lint-convert`, choose remove on one note: the `bib-parent` line stays and is empty (unchanged behaviour).\n- [ ] The message line after convert says `0 failed`; if a note is refused, the error names what would have been lost.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAMJzQKB6duQ22aU2d)_",
